{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1497277094,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwNzgwMzE3NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1564#issuecomment-307803175"},"message":"I am not in favor of progress indicators that are not based on actual evidence of progress. Why don't we relay `git clone` output itself?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1497278274,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwNzgwODk5MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1564#issuecomment-307808990"},"message":"ATM we are using GitPython's `clone_from()` method. @bpoldrack any reason not to switch to a plain `clone` cmdline call?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1523045327,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3OTM2MzM3OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1564#issuecomment-379363379"},"message":"@bpoldrack Thoughts?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1528813813,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5NjYxMDU0MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1564#issuecomment-396610540"},"message":"does plain `git clone` has any way to report progress?  on my attempt there was nothing informative and just hanged there for a while:\n```\n$\u003e git clone --progress http://datasets.datalad.org/.git\nCloning into 'datasets.datalad.org'...\n```\nthere are some git development env vars, such as GIT_TRACE which spit out some debug lines ,but I think there might be no good way to make a proper progress bar.  We could only have a \"spinning wheel\" feedback that things are \"happening\".","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1528815339,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5NjYxOTY1MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1564#issuecomment-396619650"},"message":"\u003e does plain git clone has any way to report progress? on my attempt there was nothing informative and just hanged there for a while:\n\nThere an initial \"Cloning into ...\" period where there is a hang, but then it reports progress about receiving objects.  I think you're not seeing that because the datasets repo doens't have that many objects.\n\n```\n% git clone http://datasets.datalad.org/.git\nCloning into 'datasets.datalad.org'...\n% git -C datasets.datalad.org rev-list --objects master | wc\n   2062    3760  166823\n% git clone git@github.com:datalad/datalad.git\nCloning into 'datalad'...\nremote: Counting objects: 50337, done.\nremote: Compressing objects: 100% (89/89), done.\nremote: Total 50337 (delta 70), reused 109 (delta 60), pack-reused 50188\nReceiving objects: 100% (50337/50337), 13.35 MiB | 2.92 MiB/s, done.\nResolving deltas: 100% (39529/39529), done.\n% git -C datalad rev-list --objects master | wc\n  49323   82769 2757689\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"6d482d5a11a34740eb1202233c7aa984d1782d22"},"timestamp":1528815433,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5NjYyMDEyMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1564#issuecomment-396620120"},"message":"Deleted my earlier comment because I realized it didn't make any sense, but I think the reason you're not getting any progress for http://datasets.datalad.org/.git is because it looks like it's using the \"dumb\" HTTP protocol where it just makes 1 get request per object file, and not the \"smart\" http protocol where it uses a packfile and reports progress.\n\nIt's probably work better using the git protocol (and be more bandwidth efficient too.)","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"6d482d5a11a34740eb1202233c7aa984d1782d22"},"timestamp":1528815433,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDk2MDMyNDg0"},"target":"90961dfe489a76e85f1d90e5c5d15b32b8c71e98c728fb64c9ee703fe7016d1f","message":"Deleted my earlier comment because I realized it didn't make any sense, but I think the reason you're not getting any progress for http://datasets.datalad.org/.git is because it looks like it's using the \"dumb\" HTTP protocol where it just makes 1 get request per object file, and not the \"smart\" http protocol where it uses a packfile and reports progress.\n\nIt would probably work better using the git protocol (and be more bandwidth efficient too.)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1528815546,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5NjYyMDg3Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1564#issuecomment-396620877"},"message":"\u003e but I think the reason you're not getting any progress for http://datasets.datalad.org/.git is because it looks like it's using the \"dumb\" HTTP protocol \n\n@driusan good point.  That makes more sense than my \"number of objects\" guess.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1528816720,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5NjYyODE4NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1564#issuecomment-396628184"},"message":"thank you guys!  So the question remains - either we could get any reasonable (and reliable) progress indication even if just run `git clone` ourselves ;-)  First of all it is a multistage process, where each stage ATM has (or not, like in dump http download) any progress indication","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1538504418,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTg4MDA3NTUwOA=="},"status":2}]}